1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,019
These little balls
are about to set a forest on fire.

2
00:00:03,228 --> 00:00:07,535
On purpose. A helicopter drops
them over the Georgia pines,

3
00:00:07,663 --> 00:00:11,842
and thirty to forty seconds later,
each one bursts into flame.

4
00:00:12,225 --> 00:00:16,428
In about forty-five minutes,
more than twelve hundred acres will burn.

5
00:00:16,637 --> 00:00:19,366
And above the smoke, NASA is watching.

6
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,444
This is Fort Stewart, a U.S.

7
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:23,603
Army post in southeast Georgia.

8
00:00:23,929 --> 00:00:27,470
Training on its ranges can spark
a fire at almost any time.

9
00:00:27,748 --> 00:00:31,556
So the land managers burn
the forest first, under control.

10
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:36,397
Fort Stewart uses more prescribed fire
than almost any other federal landowner.

11
00:00:36,641 --> 00:00:42,365
A prescribed fire is set on purpose,
by experts, under specific weather conditions.

12
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:46,440
Burning every two to three years
keeps the fuel on the ground low,

13
00:00:46,684 --> 00:00:50,236
so when a wildfire does start,
it can be put out easily.

14
00:00:50,678 --> 00:00:53,882
It also keeps the open forest
that rare species need,

15
00:00:54,207 --> 00:00:57,644
like the red-cockaded woodpecker
and the gopher tortoise.

16
00:00:58,247 --> 00:01:00,093
In April twenty twenty-five,

17
00:01:00,302 --> 00:01:05,306
NASA's FireSense project turned one
of these burns into an experiment.

18
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:10,101
The question: how well can aircraft
and satellites track a fire

19
00:01:10,136 --> 00:01:11,657
while it is still burning?

20
00:01:12,098 --> 00:01:13,422
It starts with the weather.

21
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:16,615
Crews check that wind
and humidity fit the plan,

22
00:01:16,742 --> 00:01:19,668
and they try to finish
before the air gets too dry.

23
00:01:20,179 --> 00:01:25,125
On the ground, a crew lights a test fire
along the edge to see how it behaves.

24
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:29,258
Once the fire has backed into the woods,
the helicopter comes in.

25
00:01:29,699 --> 00:01:32,137
Inside is a plastic sphere dispenser.

26
00:01:32,462 --> 00:01:35,098
Each ball holds potassium permanganate.

27
00:01:35,423 --> 00:01:37,524
The machine injects it with glycol,

28
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:40,740
and about thirty to forty
seconds later, it ignites.

29
00:01:41,065 --> 00:01:45,430
A grid of small, low-intensity
fires spreads across the block.

30
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:49,773
Twelve to thirteen hundred acres
burn in about forty-five minutes.

31
00:01:50,214 --> 00:01:53,593
Overhead, three crewed
aircraft carry four sensors.

32
00:01:53,801 --> 00:01:57,679
They measure the forest before,
during and after the fire,

33
00:01:57,923 --> 00:02:02,393
while satellites in orbit and sensors
on the ground add their own data.

34
00:02:02,996 --> 00:02:07,884
One of them is AVIRIS-3, built
at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory.

35
00:02:08,209 --> 00:02:10,404
A normal camera records a few colors.

36
00:02:10,729 --> 00:02:13,759
AVIRIS splits light
into hundreds of wavelengths,

37
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:16,998
and that reveals exactly
where the fire front is.

38
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:20,992
The data comes down from the plane
in three to five minutes.

39
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:25,938
On the ground, crews can see a fresh
picture of the fire every few minutes.

40
00:02:26,449 --> 00:02:29,862
Satellites might get two
to four looks at a fire per day.

41
00:02:30,245 --> 00:02:34,552
An aircraft can stay overhead
and send updates almost at once.

42
00:02:35,156 --> 00:02:39,173
On an earlier flight, the team spotted
brand-new wildfires from the air

43
00:02:39,231 --> 00:02:42,493
and sent maps to forestry
crews on the ground.

44
00:02:42,493 --> 00:02:44,327
Fire is part of these forests.

45
00:02:44,536 --> 00:02:46,440
Many of them need it to stay healthy.

46
00:02:46,765 --> 00:02:51,247
The goal is to learn how fire and smoke
really behave, so the next fire,

47
00:02:51,282 --> 00:02:54,394
planned or not, is managed
with better information.

48
00:02:54,777 --> 00:02:59,676
For another place that changes when you
see it from above, watch this one next.
